1
00:00:32,770 --> 00:00:34,640
Jensen's on the front page now
老黄又上头条了，

2
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:39,430
Oh, yeah, yeah!
哦，耶，耶！

3
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:46,860
Wall Street grades his wedding vows
华尔街忙着给他的婚姻打分。

4
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:53,140
Charts go red, the clicks go green
股价往下掉，流量往上蹿，

5
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:53,300
Oh, yeah, yeah!
哦，耶，耶！

6
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:56,600
Prime-time drama on my screen
科技新闻，硬是演成了八点档。

7
00:00:56,620 --> 00:01:00,870
He built us fast chips, then lost his own self-control
他让芯片跑得飞快，却没管住自己；

8
00:01:01,630 --> 00:01:06,820
Now suits talk of export control, bless his soul
那帮大佬倒是忙着管——管芯片往哪儿去。

9
00:01:07,610 --> 00:01:10,920
His wife deserves the truth, not a press release
老婆要的是实话，不是一篇公关稿；

10
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:14,890
But why do chips need the morals police?
可卖个芯片，还得先考思想品德？

11
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:20,220
Save a seat, my friend; fill up his glass, we've got his back
来，给老黄满上，兄弟们都在呢！

12
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:23,930
Jensen Huang, Jensen Huang, let's get back on track
老黄啊，老黄，回来接着干。

13
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:28,980
We asked for fast chips, got a late-night show
本来只想买块好显卡，结果追上了八点档；

14
00:01:29,610 --> 00:01:33,040
They can train on one tweet, then explain things they don't yet know
刷条推文就算出师，啥也不懂也敢开讲。

15
00:01:33,610 --> 00:01:37,010
All the big suits still lean on his chips; stop the blame game
大佬们还靠他的芯片吃饭，锅倒是甩得挺快；

16
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:40,910
You can't run your whole cloud on a pile of shame
光靠一堆口水，跑得动你家的服务器？

17
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:45,030
They can clone a voice, but they still can't clone that man's brain
声音倒是能克隆，老黄这脑子，你们也复制一个试试？

18
00:01:45,610 --> 00:01:48,920
Let him cook; put the boss back in the game
让他继续上菜，老黄，回来露一手！

19
00:01:59,260 --> 00:01:59,510
